winewayland: hold a role-less window's flush and expose it at the role assignment, instead of retrying it forever

The role gate (2026-09-01, Premiere's layered splash) refuses to attach a buffer to a surface that has no xdg role
yet, as xdg-shell requires. It refused by failing the flush. A failed flush keeps win32u's bounds dirty, and
win32u retries on every message-loop pass, for as long as the window has no role. A window that is never shown
never gets one.

Lightroom Classic 15.6 (clean room, nested KWin, runtime 124): its four hidden panel-drop-shadow windows
("Shadow", WS_EX_LAYERED|WS_EX_TRANSPARENT, per-pixel alpha, never shown in the session) were each flushed ~460
times a second while the app sat idle. win32u runs the alpha-shape pass before every flush, so Lightroom's UI
thread was at 45% CPU doing nothing (top -H), 90% of its samples in window_surface_flush (perf). Every click
waits behind that. The gate's own message names those windows; it appears in 63 of the operator's 65 recent
logs (Premiere, Photoshop, ...).

Now the gate consumes the flush (returns TRUE) and records that the window holds contents nothing has published
(wayland_window_surface_note_roleless). When the role is assigned, wayland_win_data_create_wayland_surface asks
for an expose of the whole window surface, which re-flushes it once the role exists: the moment the retry used to
succeed, with the same pixels. The xdg-shell rule is unchanged: no buffer is attached before the role.

Only a window that has never been shown is role-less: a hide clears the role's objects but not the role (a
Wayland surface cannot change role).

Measured:
- Lightroom: UI thread at idle 45% -> 8.6%; the shadow windows flushed 1-3 times per session instead of ~2300
  every 5 s (diagnostic count). Masking panel and flyout draw complete.
- harnesses/roleless-show.c (per-monitor aware, like Lightroom; an owned and an unowned layered window, contents
  via UpdateLayeredWindow while hidden): never-shown, NEUTRON_ROLELESS_CONSUME=0: 1570 ms of UI-thread CPU in a
  3 s idle loop; with this: 50 ms. On show, both windows display the contents given while hidden, full rects, in
  all four cases (never shown / shown-hidden-redrawn, each arm), and none of the earlier green frame.

Kill switch NEUTRON_ROLELESS_CONSUME=0 restores the retry.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
@@ -631,6 +631,9 @@
     BOOL is_fullscreen;
     BOOL managed;
     BOOL layered_attribs_set;
+    /* NEUTRON: the window surface was flushed while this window had no role; see
+     * wayland_window_surface_note_roleless() */
+    BOOL roleless_contents;
 };
 
 struct wayland_win_data *wayland_win_data_get(HWND hwnd);
@@ -648,6 +651,7 @@
 void ensure_window_surface_contents(HWND hwnd);
 BOOL wayland_window_can_commit(HWND hwnd);
 BOOL wayland_window_surface_has_role(HWND hwnd);
+BOOL wayland_window_surface_note_roleless(HWND hwnd);
 BOOL neutron_gate(const char *name, BOOL dflt);
 BOOL neutron_maxkeep_fix(void);
 
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -726,6 +726,15 @@
         break;
     }
 
+    /* NEUTRON roleless: what was flushed while the surface had no role was consumed, not committed (the role
+     * gate in wayland_window_surface_flush). Publish it now that a role exists: the expose re-flushes the whole
+     * window surface, and the flush waits for the first configure as any other would. */
+    if (role != WAYLAND_SURFACE_ROLE_NONE && data->roleless_contents && needs_expose)
+    {
+        data->roleless_contents = FALSE;
+        *needs_expose = TRUE;
+    }
+
     if (visible && client) wayland_client_surface_attach(client, data->hwnd);
     wayland_win_data_get_config(data, &surface->window);
 
@@ -2412,6 +2421,22 @@
     return has;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON roleless (2026-10-15): TRUE when the window's surface has no role, recording that it now holds
+ * contents nothing has published; the role assignment then exposes the whole window surface
+ * (wayland_win_data_create_wayland_surface). See the role gate in wayland_window_surface_flush(). */
+BOOL wayland_window_surface_note_roleless(HWND hwnd)
+{
+    struct wayland_win_data *data;
+    BOOL roleless = FALSE;
+
+    if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd))) return FALSE;
+    if (data->wayland_surface && data->wayland_surface->role == WAYLAND_SURFACE_ROLE_NONE)
+        roleless = data->roleless_contents = TRUE;
+    wayland_win_data_release(data);
+
+    return roleless;
+}
+
 BOOL wayland_window_can_commit(HWND hwnd)
 {
     struct wayland_surface *surface;
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window_surface.c
@@ -448,6 +448,25 @@
     if (!wayland_window_can_commit(window_surface->hwnd))
         return FALSE;
 
+    /* NEUTRON roleless (2026-10-15): CONSUME a flush the gate below refuses, instead of returning FALSE.
+     *
+     * FALSE keeps win32u's bounds dirty, and win32u retries on every message-loop pass -- for as long as the
+     * window has no role. A hidden window never gets one, so a hidden window with contents was flushed again on
+     * every PeekMessage for the whole session. Measured on Lightroom Classic 15.6 (clean room, nested KWin,
+     * runtime 124): its four hidden panel-drop-shadow windows ("Shadow", layered, per-pixel alpha) were each
+     * flushed ~460 times a second at idle, and the alpha-shape pass win32u runs before every flush kept the UI
+     * thread at 45% CPU doing nothing (perf: 90% of its samples in window_surface_flush). This gate's own message
+     * named the same windows; it appears in 63 of the operator's 65 recent logs, so other apps pay for it too.
+     *
+     * Consuming loses nothing: wayland_window_surface_note_roleless() records that the window holds contents
+     * nothing published, and the role assignment exposes the whole window surface (window.c,
+     * wayland_win_data_create_wayland_surface), which re-flushes it once the role exists. That is the moment the
+     * retry used to succeed, with the same pixels. The xdg-shell rule the gate enforces is unchanged.
+     *
+     * Kill switch NEUTRON_ROLELESS_CONSUME=0 restores the retry. */
+    static int roleless_consume = -1;
+    if (roleless_consume < 0) roleless_consume = neutron_gate("NEUTRON_ROLELESS_CONSUME", TRUE);
+
     /* NEUTRON: never attach a buffer to a surface that has no xdg role yet.
      *
      * MEASURED on a tester's machine 2026-09-01, 3/3 runs: for Premiere's LAYERED splash the chain
@@ -466,7 +485,16 @@
     {
         static int gate = -1;
         if (gate < 0) gate = neutron_gate("NEUTRON_ROLE_GATE", TRUE);
-        if (gate && !wayland_window_surface_has_role(window_surface->hwnd))
+        if (gate && roleless_consume && wayland_window_surface_note_roleless(window_surface->hwnd))
+        {
+            static LONG consumed;
+            if (InterlockedIncrement(&consumed) <= 20)
+                ERR("neutron-rolegate: hwnd=%p HOLDING flush -- surface has no xdg role yet "
+                    "(attaching now would violate xdg-shell); the role assignment exposes it\n",
+                    window_surface->hwnd);
+            return TRUE;
+        }
+        if (gate && !roleless_consume && !wayland_window_surface_has_role(window_surface->hwnd))
         {
             static LONG deferred;
             if (InterlockedIncrement(&deferred) <= 20)
